      "description": "Watch Sporting Kansas City vs St. Louis City highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. The atmosphere was electric as two Western Conference rivals met for a tactical duel that promised high intensity and moments of individual brilliance. Intensity and the First-Half Breakthrough On August 20, 2026 , the clash between Sporting Kansas City and St. Louis City began as a fierce battle for midfield supremacy. The match quickly turned physical, with the referee forced to issue early yellow cards to maintain order. Zorhan Bassong was the first to enter the book in the 15th minute, followed closely by Christopher Durkin in the 21st. The tension continued to simmer, and just before the break, Jansen Miller also received a caution. Just as it seemed the sides would head into the locker rooms level, St. Louis City delivered a clinical blow. In the second minute of first-half stoppage time, Eduard Loewen found the target with a composed finish. The goal completely shifted the momentum, giving the visitors a crucial lead at the interval. Consolidating the Lead and Closing Out The second half saw St. Louis City maintain their focus, and they didn't have to wait long to double their advantage. In the 56th minute, Taylor Calheira turned provider, delivering a precise assist for Calvin Harris . Harris made no mistake, firing home to put his side in a commanding position. The competitive edge remained sharp, evidenced by Conrad Wallem receiving a yellow card shortly after the hour mark. Both managers turned to their benches to manage the final stages, with St. Louis City introducing fresh legs like Alexandru Matan and Stephen Afrifa to see out the result. Despite late tactical shifts from Sporting Kansas City , the visitors remained disciplined until the final whistle, securing a vital three points in the MLS standings."
